# Git attributes: how Git stores, checks out and diffs files.
#
# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every OS, overriding
# a local core.autocrlf, so the working tree matches what rustfmt
# (newline_style in rustfmt.toml), Prettier and .editorconfig expect. After
# changing the rules below, run `git add --renormalize .` and commit the
# result.

# Files Git detects as text: LF in the repository and in the working tree.
# Cargo.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml and SVG files are text too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rust sources are always text, whatever Git's detection says.
*.rs text eol=lf

# The one exception: cmd.exe can fail to find `goto` and `call` labels in a
# batch file with LF line endings, so batch files are checked out with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Source and configuration files are always diffed as text. Git treats any
# file containing a NUL byte as binary, so `git diff` would print only "Binary
# files differ" and hide a change that still ships (rustc accepts a NUL inside
# a comment). Plain `diff` turns that detection off; a named driver such as
# `diff=rust` does not. It is not set on `*`, which would print real binary
# files as text.

# Code, including SVG (it can carry scripts), SQL migrations, scripts and
# Windows application manifests (they request privileges).
*.rs diff
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.mts diff
*.cts diff
*.js diff
*.mjs diff
*.cjs diff
*.vue diff
*.html diff
*.css diff
*.svg diff
*.sql diff
*.ps1 diff
*.bat diff
*.cmd diff
*.manifest diff

# Configuration, lockfiles, the WiX installer sources, licenses, and Markdown
# (agents follow the docs as instructions).
*.json diff
*.jsonc diff
*.toml diff
*.yml diff
*.yaml diff
*.md diff
*.wxs diff
*.wxi diff
*.wxl diff
*.wixproj diff
Cargo.lock diff
justfile diff
.npmrc diff
.editorconfig diff
.gitattributes diff
.gitignore diff
CODEOWNERS diff
LICENSE-* diff

# Binary files: never converted, diffed or merged as text. Git usually detects
# them on its own; listing them guarantees that a line-ending conversion can
# never corrupt one.

# Images and icons: app, tray and extension icons, mockups, installer bitmaps.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary

# Fonts: Geist and Geist Mono are bundled with the app.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Sounds, documents and archives.
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Windows and installer binaries (build output, normally ignored).
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.msi binary
*.cab binary
